  "worked_solution": "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{2}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\pi =\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{\\pi }=1.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $2$ unit up. Hence, $D=2.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=1+2=3.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)+2.\n$$",
